          "y": 210,
          "size": 30,
          "color": "yellow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "id": "cg",
          "latex": "\\frac{\\textcolor{#B08CD9}{9-1}}{\\textcolor{#83C167}{3-1}} = \\frac{\\textcolor{#B08CD9}{8}}{\\textcolor{#83C167}{2}} = \\textcolor{#FFE45C}{4}",
          "x": 1290,
          "y": 300,
          "size": 44
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "id": "ask",
          "text": "Is the curve at P\nas steep as 4?",
          "x": 1290,
          "y": 470,
          "size": 34
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "id": "ans",
          "text": "No: near P the curve is\nflatter than the chord.",
          "x": 1290,
          "y": 620,
          "size": 30
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "id": "avg",
          "text": "A chord gives an average,\nlike the car's 8 m/s.",
          "x": 1290,
          "y": 740,
          "size": 28,
          "color": "grey"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "narration": "A straight line has one gradient everywhere, but a curve keeps getting steeper. Here's y = x², the same shape as the car's journey.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "ax",
                "curve"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "Our question, in maths: how steep is this curve exactly at P, where x = 1?",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "p",
                "p_l"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "We only know how to measure straight lines, so pick a second point Q at x = 3 and join them. This yellow line is called a chord.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "q",
                "q_l",
                "chord"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "From P to Q we go 2 across and 8 up.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "run",
                "run_l",
                "rise",
                "rise_l"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "So the chord's gradient is 8 over 2, which is 4.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "cg_t",
                "cg"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "Is the curve at P really as steep as 4? Look closely at P before you answer.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "ask"
              ]
            },
            {
              "do": "indicate",
              "ids": [
                "p"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "narration": "No: near P the curve is flatter than the chord. The chord only gives an average, just like the car's 8 metres per second.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "do": "show",
              "ids": [
                "ans",
                "avg"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
